# skyeCladach — Uathach on the shore of Skye
#
# The player's first conversation on the island. The lesson itself (the
# step drill, her dust-dash, the bramble lane) is run by the scene, and
# her lines during it are captions, not cards -- see
# js/game/scenes/locations/skye/skyeCladach.js. This draft is only what
# she says when you tap her.
#
# NOTES USED
#   drill_start            -> "Ready." chosen; the scene starts the drill
#   drill_done             -> (scene) drill finished
#   lesson_movement        -> (scene) reached her at the top of the lane
#   uathach_told_machaire  -> she has pointed them onward
#   climb_clean / climb_rough -> (scene) how the climb went, before the pep talk
#   go_loch / go_garden    -> pep-talk choice; one-off, the scene clears it
#   pep_done               -> (scene) the pep talk is over
#
# IRISH IS A FIRST DRAFT -- check before shipping.

@file skye/skyeCladach


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — the landing
@continue
So. The sea gave you up.
% Bhuel. Scaoil an fharraige uaithi thú.
I am Uathach, daughter of Scáthach.
% Is mise Uathach, iníon Scáthaí.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1 — first, an order
@when !note drill_start
@hold
@again Well? / Bhuel?
My mother is waiting at the dún.
% Tá mo mháthair ag fanacht ag an dún.
But first, let's see if you can follow an order.
% Ach ar dtús, feicfimid an féidir leat ordú a leanúint.

* Ready.
% Réidh.
@note drill_start
@exit

* Who is Scáthach?
% Cé hí Scáthach?
@first
> Who is Scáthach?
% Cé hí Scáthach?
< The finest teacher of arms in the world.
% An múinteoir arm is fearr ar domhan.
< And the hardest.
% Agus an ceann is crua.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE PEP TALK -- at the top of the wall, opened by the scene. It sets
# climb_clean (a correction or none) or climb_rough first. The subtext is
# the whole project: you came, and that matters. She never says so.
= node 1a — the top, a clean climb
@when note climb_clean
@when !note pep_done
@hold
You didn't miss a step.
% Níor chaill tú céim.
Welcome to Skye. Not many come this way. You did.
% Fáilte go Scí. Ní thagann mórán an bealach seo. Tháinig tusa.
If that was easy, on we go. If you want more, there's always more.
% Más furasta a bhí sé, ar aghaidh linn. Más mian leat tuilleadh, bíonn tuilleadh ann i gcónaí.

* On to the loch.
% Ar aghaidh chuig an loch.
@note go_loch
@exit

* To the garden first.
% Chuig an ngairdín ar dtús.
@note go_garden
@exit


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1b — the top, a harder climb
@when note climb_rough
@when !note pep_done
@hold
That wasn't easy. No matter.
% Ní raibh sé sin éasca. Is cuma.
Welcome to Skye. Not many come this way. You did.
% Fáilte go Scí. Ní thagann mórán an bealach seo. Tháinig tusa.
There's a garden over west. We'll practise there as long as you like.
% Tá gairdín thiar ansin. Cleachtfaimid ann chomh fada agus is mian leat.

* To the garden.
% Chuig an ngairdín.
@note go_garden
@exit

* On to the loch.
% Ar aghaidh chuig an loch.
@note go_loch
@exit


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 2 — mid-lesson
@when note drill_start
@when !note lesson_movement
@hold
Listen, and move.
% Éist, agus bog.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 3 — onward
@when note lesson_movement
@when !note uathach_told_machaire
@note uathach_told_machaire
@continue
Beyond is the machaire. The other students idle there.
% Thall ansin tá an machaire. Bíonn na daltaí eile ag díomhaoineas ann.
Feardiad will show you how things are done here.
% Taispeánfaidh Feardiad duit conas a dhéantar rudaí anseo.
Past them is the long bridge, and my mother beyond it.
% Taobh thall díobh tá an droichead fada, agus mo mháthair ar an taobh eile de.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 4 — after
@when note uathach_told_machaire
@hold
Go on. I'll not carry you.
% Ar aghaidh leat. Ní iompróidh mé thú.
